[{"current_page":20,"data":[{"id":177,"user_id":1,"type":"Tool","sub_type":"Text","title":"Bard","publisher":null,"authors":"DeepMind","featuring":null,"publish_date":"2023-01-02","link":"https:\/\/bard.google.com\/","content":"<p>DeepMind's LLM 'based on a lightweight and optimized version of LaMDA' which has been 'pre-trained on a variety of data from publicly available sources'. It is available for public use, but the model and training data themselves remain inaccessible.<\/p>","contact":"AM","permission_status":null,"license":null,"example":null,"source":null,"editors":null,"image":null,"is_visible":1,"created_at":"2023-01-27T08:57:36.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-09-08T23:41:24.000000Z","pinned":0},{"id":176,"user_id":1,"type":"Tool","sub_type":"3D","title":"Avalon","publisher":null,"authors":"Generally Intelligence","featuring":null,"publish_date":"2022-01-02","link":"https:\/\/generallyintelligent.com\/avalon\/","content":"<p>Avalon in a procedurally-generated training environment for Reinforcement Learning Agents toward the goal of 'generalization' developed by Generally Intelligent. It is open source and built on the (also OS) Godot game engine. GI have a good research output on their website which helps to scaffold the tools development and use.<\/p>","contact":"AM","permission_status":null,"license":"GPL-3.0","example":null,"source":null,"editors":null,"image":null,"is_visible":1,"created_at":"2023-01-27T08:57:36.000000Z","updated_at":"2023-09-08T23:47:05.000000Z","pinned":0},{"id":175,"user_id":1,"type":"Tool","sub_type":"Text","title":"Langchain","publisher":null,"authors":"hwchase17","featuring":null,"publish_date":"2022-01-02","link":"https:\/\/github.com\/hwchase17\/langchain\/","content":"<p>Langchain is an open source project which aims to enable LLM 'composability', making the core affordances of NLP more applicable in specific contexts. It works to improve LLM interoperability, accepting community contributions to development.<\/p>","contact":"AM"